WEBVTT

00:00:03.180 --> 00:00:05.920
It's obviously a hoax.

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:08.860
We don't know for sure.

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:12.640
Only a few know about the Ignis’ existence.

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:15.380
Wait up, Earth!

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:17.340
What do you want with me?

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:22.320
Duel me, Playmaker.

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.000
Duel you?

00:00:24.620 --> 00:00:27.220
I want to ask you something.

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:28.500
Ask me?

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:31.420
We’re searching for a man named Bohman.

00:00:31.420 --> 00:00:35.450
He stole my acquaintance’s 
brother’s consciousness data.

00:00:35.860 --> 00:00:40.460
And he seems to be linked to 
Cyberse World’s destruction.

00:00:40.770 --> 00:00:45.200
If you want to ask for that info, duel me.

00:00:45.580 --> 00:00:48.560
Earth was great at dueling!

00:00:48.560 --> 00:00:50.330
Link Summon!

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:53.040
Appear, Link 2!

00:00:56.160 --> 00:00:59.470
G Golem Crystal Heart!

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:09.380
This isn’t a monster effect.

00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:15.970
It's time to verify humanity 
and AI’s future.

00:01:32.280 --> 00:01:38.290
Our lives aren't forever

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:45.080
We wander, searching for the meaning of life

00:01:46.030 --> 00:01:52.400
Even if it's not the right direction, 
just keep looking forward

00:01:52.850 --> 00:01:58.980
Sharing hope for the future

00:01:58.980 --> 00:02:05.720
tell me  We're searching for 
memories lost in the darkness

00:02:05.920 --> 00:02:12.960
I feel your flame  Your 
impulses pierce the light

00:02:13.090 --> 00:02:19.660
I want to share your pain

00:02:55.820 --> 00:02:57.790
You wanted to talk to me?

00:02:58.710 --> 00:03:00.260
Come closer.

00:03:00.260 --> 00:03:02.000
Huh?  Okay.

00:03:04.780 --> 00:03:08.440
I need to tell you something.

00:03:09.260 --> 00:03:12.880
Wait!  My heart isn’t ready!  I-

00:03:12.880 --> 00:03:16.010
The Cyberse World will soon break apart.

00:03:17.680 --> 00:03:20.290
The Cyberse World will break apart?

00:03:20.290 --> 00:03:21.110
Yes.

00:03:21.110 --> 00:03:27.800
We must soon choose whether to 
coexist or split from the humans.

00:03:28.120 --> 00:03:30.800
Is that true?

00:03:30.800 --> 00:03:33.120
Wait, that’s a silly question.

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:36.800
You have the power to differentiate 
between lies and truth.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:38.270
Yes.

00:03:40.440 --> 00:03:42.960
Which side will you join?

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:44.720
I can’t tell you.

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:48.630
Why?  I'll join the side you choose.

00:03:48.630 --> 00:03:49.720
That’s why.

00:03:50.040 --> 00:03:53.380
Are humans the Ignis' allies?

00:03:53.380 --> 00:03:56.560
You must decide on your own.

00:04:00.040 --> 00:04:01.320
Take this.

00:04:04.820 --> 00:04:06.220
This is…

00:04:08.080 --> 00:04:10.190
Crystal Heart.

00:04:10.190 --> 00:04:12.710
For which side to join...

00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:15.500
Determine with your own eyes.

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:18.510
What's humanity and AI's future?

00:04:18.510 --> 00:04:21.020
What's the truth?

00:04:28.380 --> 00:04:30.860
I'll find the answer in this duel.

00:04:30.860 --> 00:04:33.830
G Golem Crystal Heart’s effect!

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:42.950
Once per turn, it Special Summons and 
co-links an Earth Link Monster from my graveyard!

00:04:43.390 --> 00:04:48.340
Resurrect!  G Golem Invalid Dolmen!

00:04:53.450 --> 00:04:58.080
Then I place a G Golem 
Counter on Crystal Heart.

00:04:58.410 --> 00:05:05.690
For every G Golem Counter, the Earth 
monster next to its link gains 600 ATK!

00:05:08.470 --> 00:05:09.490
Battle!

00:05:09.490 --> 00:05:14.700
G Golem Invalid Dolmen 
attacks Zombie Prosaber!

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:23.530
I end my turn.

00:05:23.530 --> 00:05:27.010
He makes sure to shave away LP!

00:05:27.330 --> 00:05:29.750
My turn!  I draw!

00:05:29.750 --> 00:05:33.210
I summon Clock Wyvern from my hand!

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:40.360
Clock Wyvern’s effect!

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:48.190
Once per turn, by halving its ATK, it 
Special Summons a Clock Token in defense position!

00:05:48.190 --> 00:05:51.760
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:05:53.260 --> 00:05:56.370
The summoning condition 
is one Level 1 monster!

00:05:56.370 --> 00:05:59.940
I set Clock Token in the Link Marker!

00:06:01.170 --> 00:06:02.320
Link Summon!

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:06.220
Appear, Link 1 Linkuriboh!

00:06:06.220 --> 00:06:11.020
From my hand, I activate 
the spell card, Link Back!

00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:18.540
A Link Monster in the Extra Monster Zone 
moves to my Main Monster Zone next to its link.

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:22.250
Then for each of its Link Markers...

00:06:22.250 --> 00:06:25.500
...I send a card from the top 
of my deck to the graveyard.

00:06:25.840 --> 00:06:31.130
From my hand, I activate the 
spell card, Cynet Fusion!

00:06:31.130 --> 00:06:37.720
I send Fusion Materials from my hand and 
field to Special Summon the Fusion Monster!

00:06:38.260 --> 00:06:41.720
I send Clock Wyvern and 
Linkuriboh to the graveyard.

00:06:42.240 --> 00:06:45.890
When there are no monsters 
in my Extra Monster Zone...

00:06:45.890 --> 00:06:51.460
...I can banish a Cyberse Link Monster from 
my graveyard and use it as Fusion Material!

00:06:51.460 --> 00:06:54.930
I banish Zombie Prosaber!

00:06:57.250 --> 00:06:59.130
Fusion Summon!

00:06:59.130 --> 00:07:02.910
Come out!  Cyberse Clock Dragon!

00:07:11.150 --> 00:07:13.150
Fusion Summon!

00:07:13.150 --> 00:07:17.130
See that!  Playmaker can even do this!

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:20.960
When Cyberse Clock Dragon 
is Fusion Summoned...

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:24.480
...I send a card from the top 
of my deck to the graveyard for

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:27.510
every Fusion Material Link Monster's Marker.

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:31.240
And it gains 1000 ATK per card!

00:07:31.240 --> 00:07:34.820
I send two cards from my 
deck to the graveyard!

00:07:35.510 --> 00:07:37.600
Cyberse Clockup!

00:07:39.840 --> 00:07:42.320
4500 ATK!

00:07:42.630 --> 00:07:43.650
Battle!

00:07:43.650 --> 00:07:49.520
Cyberse Clock Dragon attacks 
G Golem Crystal Heart!

00:07:49.520 --> 00:07:52.390
Crystal Heart has 0 ATK!

00:07:52.390 --> 00:07:55.420
With this strike, Playmaker wins!

00:07:55.420 --> 00:07:56.920
No, he won’t win!

00:07:58.110 --> 00:08:01.010
G Golem Invalid Dolmen’s effect!

00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:06.470
As long as it's on the field, you 
can only attack Invalid Dolmen.

00:08:06.470 --> 00:08:07.540
What?

00:08:17.390 --> 00:08:20.220
G Golem Invalid Dolmen’s effect!

00:08:20.220 --> 00:08:27.760
When it's destroyed, it negates 
all your faceup cards' effects!

00:08:32.720 --> 00:08:36.460
Clock Dragon’s ATK returned to normal!

00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:39.420
Playmaker is incredibly strong.

00:08:39.420 --> 00:08:44.240
Is the Dark Ignis siding with him 
to take advantage of his power?

00:08:44.240 --> 00:08:45.420
Or…

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:47.370
I end my turn.

00:08:47.370 --> 00:08:53.380
It’s as if that monster sacrificed 
itself to protect Aqua’s monster.

00:08:54.360 --> 00:08:56.580
I see!  I get it!

00:08:56.580 --> 00:08:57.320
Get what?

00:08:57.320 --> 00:09:02.280
During the time I was 
still in Cyberse World...

00:09:06.780 --> 00:09:09.760
Linkuriboh!  Jump in there!

00:09:12.130 --> 00:09:15.220
I said Aqua liked me, right?

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:19.200
It’s dangerous!  Please stop!

00:09:19.200 --> 00:09:21.940
Don’t worry!

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:41.760
That was close!

00:09:42.280 --> 00:09:44.480
How many times must I tell you!

00:09:44.860 --> 00:09:47.440
You're an Ignis!  Act like one!

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:49.680
Sorry.

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:54.000
I think Earth didn’t like that.

00:09:58.620 --> 00:10:01.860
Stay away from the Water Ignis!

00:10:02.700 --> 00:10:05.060
I'll protect her!

00:10:05.060 --> 00:10:08.340
Did I need to hear this story right now?

00:10:08.340 --> 00:10:13.540
Definitely!  It means his deck is 
full of his feelings towards Aqua.

00:10:13.540 --> 00:10:18.480
If Earth is an AI that fully 
understands human emotions...

00:10:18.480 --> 00:10:21.140
He’ll be very dangerous.

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:24.840
My turn!  I draw!

00:10:29.300 --> 00:10:32.240
I won’t let you lay a finger on Aqua.

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:35.500
G Golem Crystal Heart’s effect!

00:10:35.500 --> 00:10:43.960
It Special Summons and co-links an 
Earth Link Monster from my graveyard.

00:10:44.480 --> 00:10:48.980
Resurrect!  G Golem Invalid Dolmen!

00:10:56.740 --> 00:11:01.880
Then I place a G Golem 
Counter on Crystal Heart.

00:11:01.880 --> 00:11:09.400
For every G Golem Counter, an Earth 
monster next to its link gains 600 ATK!

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:15.140
4000 ATK?

00:11:15.700 --> 00:11:16.740
Battle!

00:11:17.040 --> 00:11:23.700
G Golem Invalid Dolmen attacks 
Cyberse Clock Dragon!

00:11:28.100 --> 00:11:29.600
That was close!

00:11:29.600 --> 00:11:32.160
Barely safe with 100 LP!

00:11:36.800 --> 00:11:40.610
Hey, Playmaker!  Pull yourself together!

00:11:40.610 --> 00:11:44.200
Since I'm on your side, 
this is a pathetic showing!

00:11:44.200 --> 00:11:47.420
You’re gonna let him pummel you?

00:11:47.780 --> 00:11:51.400
You’re irresponsible but calculating.

00:11:51.400 --> 00:11:56.620
If this is the human you selected, 
it won’t end this easily.

00:11:56.620 --> 00:12:00.100
G Golem Crystal Heart’s effect!

00:12:00.100 --> 00:12:08.440
When it has at least two G Golem Counters, 
co-linked Link Monsters can attack twice!

00:12:09.380 --> 00:12:11.460
It can attack again?

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:14.920
That means we’ll lose to a direct attack!

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:17.220
That’s bad acting.

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:23.360
Battle!  G Golem Invalid Dolmen 
attacks Playmaker directly!

00:12:23.720 --> 00:12:27.100
I activate the Quick-Play Spell, Spool Code!

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:34.140
When your monster attacks me directly, if I 
have at least three Cyberses in my graveyard...

00:12:34.140 --> 00:12:36.760
...that attack is negated!

00:12:38.740 --> 00:12:44.980
Then I can Special Summon up to three Spool 
Tokens on my field in defense position!

00:12:49.300 --> 00:12:53.100
Ai, your overacting had the opposite effect.

00:12:54.520 --> 00:12:56.100
He knew I was acting?

00:12:56.100 --> 00:12:57.340
Of course.

00:13:00.100 --> 00:13:02.530
You're so confident that you can smirk now?

00:13:03.100 --> 00:13:07.230
Playmaker, why are you with Ai?

00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:13.920
To me, it looks like he’s holding you back.

00:13:13.920 --> 00:13:14.940
Hey!

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:18.980
Just when I thought we were 
getting closer, you diss me?

00:13:18.980 --> 00:13:20.940
Why are we together?

00:13:20.940 --> 00:13:24.680
Because we’re irreplaceable partners!

00:13:25.060 --> 00:13:27.680
I never thought of him as a partner.

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:30.160
Still no?

00:13:30.840 --> 00:13:34.060
There are three reasons I’m with him.

00:13:34.060 --> 00:13:37.400
One: We both have things we must do.

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:42.760
Two: To do it, we have mutual 
enemies we must find.

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:47.740
Three: That’s why we’re 
together with our own free will.

00:13:47.740 --> 00:13:49.260
Playmaker!

00:13:49.260 --> 00:13:51.500
If that makes us partners…

00:13:51.500 --> 00:13:53.830
You're able to do that?

00:13:53.830 --> 00:13:57.560
If my partner's going overboard, so will I!

00:13:59.020 --> 00:14:00.780
…then call us that.

00:14:01.680 --> 00:14:03.460
Playmaker…

00:14:03.460 --> 00:14:06.480
C'mon, be honest with yourself.

00:14:06.480 --> 00:14:10.460
I set two cards and end my turn.

00:14:10.460 --> 00:14:13.200
My turn!  I draw!

00:14:13.200 --> 00:14:16.200
Playmaker only has 100 LP left.

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:19.160
He will try to finish me this turn!

00:14:19.160 --> 00:14:22.960
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:14:23.700 --> 00:14:27.180
The summoning conditions are two Cyberses!

00:14:27.180 --> 00:14:31.170
I set two Spool Tokens in the Link Markers!

00:14:31.500 --> 00:14:33.120
Link Summon!

00:14:33.120 --> 00:14:37.180
Appear, Link 2 Clock Lizard!

00:14:38.320 --> 00:14:42.600
Appear again!  The circuit 
that leads to the future!

00:14:42.600 --> 00:14:47.740
The summoning condition is 
one Level 4 or lower Cyberse!

00:14:49.900 --> 00:14:51.240
Link Summon!

00:14:51.900 --> 00:14:57.140
Appear!  Link 1 Link Devotee!

00:14:57.460 --> 00:15:00.880
I activate the Continuous Spell, Link Drive!

00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:04.620
I tribute a Link Monster on my field.

00:15:04.620 --> 00:15:10.820
You take 500 damage for 
each of its Link Markers!

00:15:14.320 --> 00:15:19.100
When Link Devotee is tributed 
while it’s co-linked...

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:24.340
...I can Special Summon two Link Tokens 
on my field in defense position!

00:15:24.340 --> 00:15:28.060
Appear!  The circuit that 
leads to the future!

00:15:29.970 --> 00:15:32.380
Playmaker can’t be stopped!

00:15:32.380 --> 00:15:34.360
Here he comes!

00:15:34.360 --> 00:15:37.100
The summoning conditions are two monsters!

00:15:37.100 --> 00:15:41.060
I set two Link Tokens in the Link Markers!

00:15:42.920 --> 00:15:44.020
Link Summon!

00:15:44.020 --> 00:15:48.860
Appear!  Link 2 Security Dragon!

00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:55.680
Security Dragon’s effect activates!

00:15:55.680 --> 00:15:59.680
One monster on your field 
returns to your hand!

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:04.620
I select G Golem Invalid Dolmen!

00:16:04.620 --> 00:16:06.580
This is the end!

00:16:06.580 --> 00:16:13.340
When Invalid Dolmen is co-linked, 
your monsters can't affect it!

00:16:18.680 --> 00:16:20.020
Too bad.

00:16:20.580 --> 00:16:26.000
No one can destroy Invalid 
Dolmen’s solid defense!

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:28.880
What are you talking about, Earth?

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:30.760
We're just warming up.

00:16:30.760 --> 00:16:32.000
The real show…

00:16:32.000 --> 00:16:32.960
…begins now!

00:16:34.370 --> 00:16:37.620
I tribute Clock Lizard 
to activate its effect!

00:16:37.620 --> 00:16:42.600
I return a Fusion Monster in 
my graveyard to my Extra Deck!

00:16:42.920 --> 00:16:46.320
I return Cyberse Clock Dragon!

00:16:46.820 --> 00:16:54.060
And by banishing the required Fusion 
Materials from my graveyard, I can Fusion Summon!

00:16:54.060 --> 00:16:57.020
You can still Fusion Summon?

00:16:57.020 --> 00:17:02.270
I banish Clock Wyvern, Link 2 
Clock Lizard, Link 1 Linkuriboh

00:17:02.270 --> 00:17:07.510
and Link Devotee from my 
graveyard to Fusion Summon!

00:17:07.510 --> 00:17:09.040
Fusion Summon!

00:17:11.510 --> 00:17:15.600
Appear again, Cyberse Clock Dragon!

00:17:20.240 --> 00:17:21.960
Welcome back!

00:17:22.620 --> 00:17:26.420
When Cyberse Clock Dragon 
is Fusion Summoned...

00:17:26.420 --> 00:17:30.960
...I send a card from the top of my deck to the 
graveyard for every Fusion Materials' Link Marker.

00:17:30.960 --> 00:17:34.520
And it gains 1000 ATK per card!

00:17:34.520 --> 00:17:38.320
I send four cards from 
my deck to the graveyard!

00:17:38.320 --> 00:17:40.770
Cyberse Clockup!

00:17:40.770 --> 00:17:43.270
6500 ATK!

00:17:43.270 --> 00:17:46.500
You'll end him with a single 
strike this time, Playmaker!

00:17:46.500 --> 00:17:48.410
No, not yet!

00:17:48.410 --> 00:17:52.620
I activate the trap card, 
Gravity Fluctuation!

00:17:52.620 --> 00:17:56.600
I destroy an Earth monster on my field.

00:17:56.600 --> 00:18:01.990
You must choose a monster with 
equal or lower ATK and destroy it!

00:18:01.990 --> 00:18:06.800
I destroy G Golem Invalid Dolmen!

00:18:08.660 --> 00:18:11.900
Now choose which monster to destroy!

00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:17.380
I destroy... Security Dragon!

00:18:19.180 --> 00:18:29.080
When Invalid Dolmen is destroyed, it 
negates all faceup cards on your field!

00:18:30.400 --> 00:18:35.080
Clock Dragon’s ATK was 
returned to normal again.

00:18:35.080 --> 00:18:39.030
But now… Crystal Heart is defenseless!

00:18:39.030 --> 00:18:40.560
Battle!

00:18:40.560 --> 00:18:45.000
Cyberse Clock Dragon attacks Crystal Heart!

00:18:45.000 --> 00:18:48.480
I activate the trap card, Love Gravity!

00:18:48.480 --> 00:18:53.940
I Special Summon an Earth Link Monster 
next to a Link Monster’s link!

00:18:54.340 --> 00:18:57.420
Resurrect!  Invalid Dolmen!

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:04.120
You protected it?  You 
must really care for Aqua!

00:19:04.560 --> 00:19:07.640
G Golem Crystal Heart’s effect!

00:19:07.640 --> 00:19:15.330
For every counter on this monster, an Earth 
monster next to its link gain 600 ATK!

00:19:15.620 --> 00:19:20.070
I told you that Invalid 
Dolmen’s defense is perfect!

00:19:20.070 --> 00:19:24.180
I won’t let you lay a 
finger on Crystal Heart!

00:19:24.180 --> 00:19:26.000
Yeah, I know.

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:30.720
My banished Clock Lizard's effect!

00:19:30.720 --> 00:19:35.740
Monsters that were Special 
Summoned to your field...

00:19:35.740 --> 00:19:40.340
...lose 400 ATK for every Cyberse 
in my graveyard this turn!

00:19:40.340 --> 00:19:44.540
Umm…  There are ten 
Cyberses in the graveyard!

00:19:44.540 --> 00:19:45.800
That means…

00:19:46.180 --> 00:19:50.040
Invalid Dolmen loses 4000 ATK!

00:19:54.140 --> 00:19:57.850
Aww!  All that work to get to 
4000, but it’s down to 0!

00:19:57.850 --> 00:20:00.180
You anticipated all this?

00:20:00.180 --> 00:20:01.650
Battle!

00:20:01.650 --> 00:20:06.620
Cyberse Clock Dragon attacks 
G Golem Invalid Dolmen!

00:20:07.620 --> 00:20:10.780
Pulse Pressure!

00:20:34.660 --> 00:20:37.820
I lose.

00:20:38.120 --> 00:20:42.240
But congrats on protecting Aqua to the end.

00:20:43.320 --> 00:20:47.060
As you promised, tell us about Bohman.

00:20:47.060 --> 00:20:48.640
I know.

00:20:49.240 --> 00:20:51.260
Bohman went to…

00:20:51.260 --> 00:20:52.600
Yeah?

00:20:52.600 --> 00:20:54.300
I don’t know anything.

00:20:55.040 --> 00:20:57.020
What’s with that!

00:20:57.020 --> 00:21:00.020
And it’s the first time 
I heard the name Bohman.

00:21:00.020 --> 00:21:02.720
That’s not what we agreed to!

00:21:02.720 --> 00:21:07.320
You said if we dueled, you’d 
give us info on Bohman!

00:21:07.320 --> 00:21:13.000
And I gave you info that “I don’t 
know anything” about Bohman.

00:21:13.000 --> 00:21:16.000
That’s not fair!

00:21:16.000 --> 00:21:17.900
I answered honestly.

00:21:19.800 --> 00:21:22.460
My business is done.  Leave.

00:21:22.940 --> 00:21:27.020
Hey, wait!  We're not done talking!

00:21:34.280 --> 00:21:36.400
Aww, c'mon!

00:21:36.400 --> 00:21:39.900
We only dueled to help Earth kill time!

00:21:39.900 --> 00:21:42.020
What a joke!

